{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins","id":112142,"title":"Crossover Brainstorm: Various Shan'iatu Origins.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-13T11:30:13-07:00","id":112142,"title":"Crossover Brainstorm: Various Shan'iatu Origins.","content":"Okay so no need to worry, this thread is not trying to figure out the actual origin of the Shan'iatu. Its an attempt to come up with different methods to fill in the setting without waiting for other mummy books, and using the rest of the NWOD as a resource.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please feel free to discuss your own takes on these, suggested ideas or tweaks, new ideas, and preferred methods of use. If you don't like crossover stuff well you don't have to participate, this isn't expected to be a standard game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My first idea was to make the Shan'iatu a 3rd Tier Krew of Sineaters with the Judges as their Geist. There various sorcery is composed of their Keys and Dominions, and the high magic they use to do unique things are High Level Ceremony, with level 9 and Ten rituals used to make Gods and Immortals. They used their connections with the dead to catalog and find relics, and eventually develop Ceremonies to make their own, and teach mortals Merits so they can make them for them as well. Necromancy seemed to be the Shan'iatu's specialty but they also showed other wizardy tricks like elemental mastery, and the knowing of secrets. This would also put Sineaters as natural members of the Guilds, and perhaps ancient Dominions and Keys for things such as alchemy, and slavery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One idea I didn't take time to consider because of how obvious it is is to use them as Mages. Would you make them the latest iteration of a group trying to remake the Nameless city? Or would they be true Pre Atlantis? Or Hell what is wrong with making Irem Atlantis? The default Shan'iatu seem to be remanents of a more Ancient Secret so they may even be from a prehuman civilization? Would you have them contain Archmages? Would they be Exarch Related? They could even be the Exarchs themselves, I wouldn't mind a story exploring that idea. 42 mages is a large number, a whole consilium so even if they were all Masters that would be insanely impressive, and if they contained at least one Archmage per guild that would also be impressive. But perhaps the Gods of Irem are Archmages and the Shan'iatu being the Earthly mages preparing Omens and seeking Ascension. What twists would you take on this? Their magics could explain all the feats, and Imperial Magic could make for the Rite of Return and the conquering of the Duat. Maybe the Duat could even be a Supernal realm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ancient Changelings would be a very interesting take, maybe the Judges where their Keepers, or the Fates the Wyrd has in store for Each Shan'iatu to become? Relics after all most closely resemble Tokens, so maybe their is some connection there. Perhaps the Nameless Gods are beings they encountered that aren't Fae, much like the Seasons and other patrons of Courts. Perhaps the Duat is actually in Arcadia? Perhaps solely accessible through Underground Hedge Paths in the Desert? Perhaps they have a connection to the Lost Pantheon, with members of the Ancient serving as the Gods of Irem? A lot of Irem could be developed just by a group of High Wyrd Beings with Social and Mental traits above 5, not to mention Contract use, pacts and Goblin MArket/Contracts providing pretty much all the magic they need.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What if the Shan'iatu are the Maggot Host, Shartha that Father Wolf Chased into the Underworld. Perhaps they chose not become one and chose other goals for themselves, or perhaps they could not even become One, and thus had to decide another goal to fill their final drive. Perhaps they are an origin of Vampires animating the dead with Larvae, that would evolve into Revanents and Vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if the Shan'iatu were simply Mortals with Supernatural Merits? Mortals can make Relics, and various supernatural merits can do a wide range of supernatural effects, particularly if they are long lived and have grown a vast amount of secrets. And Relics themselves could cover insanely potent feats, so perhaps the magic is just the cultivating of human projects towards supernatural ends, after all that explains most of the God Machines feats and it can do things like mass extinction and time travel. They could even have been a Hunter Conspiracy, After all we already have Relics as an Endowment, as well as Alchemy. Maybe they were something like a Conspiracy with 7 Conspiracies/Endowments working together. Hell I could see them having connections to the Aegis Kai, The Cheiron Group, and the Ascending Ones! Uter and Alchemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if they are Ghosts/Revanents from a fallen civilization? Using various Ghostly Numina and Influence, and cultivating Relics. Much like the Mortal option much can be explained with Relics, human nations turned to arcane ends, and the little cheat of Numina and Influence.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then there is the idea of the Priests being a conspiracy of various beings, and the Arisen and Irem could be a product of the Synthesis of multiple dark Secrets. After all everyone seems to fancy being a god, or to conquer. These are simple goals. Relics before Mummy where already the general default magic item of the NWOD. The Power of Werewolf Rites, Supernal Magic, The Wyrd, Ceremonies, and other Secrets combined could do some scary stuff if they worked towards the same goals.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and additions? What would be some fun angles to Run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T06:49:30-07:00","id":112598,"title":"","content":"In my own canon, they're aliens. Straight up. I don't know what the ramifications are of that and I'm not too worried about it. My planned long-term campaign even has a crystal skull of a Shan'iatu as being the crucial game-changing relic the <i>Mummy</i> world is going crazy for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T06:57:10-07:00","id":112601,"title":"","content":"I made Duat a section of the Abyss. The Sorcerer-Kings-Judge-Gods are kind of anti-mages who draw their power from the dark magics of the abyss through suffering, and &quot;ascended&quot; into becoming abyssal gods themselves.<br /> <br /> As such, this makes the Nameless Empire one of the Barbarian Cities that Atlantis went to war with. Along with the old Sumerian Werewolf one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:02:00-07:00","id":112609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins#post112142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first idea was to make the Shan'iatu a 3rd Tier Krew of Sineaters with the Judges as their Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably my favourite among the candidates from other game lines. Sineaters are more mystically powerful than the Shan'iatu appeared to be, but that could be refined to more mystically powerful <i>now</i>. Just as Irem was the first civilisation, perhaps the Shan'iatu were the first major krewe, and marked the beginning of the development of many of the Sineater powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One idea I didn't take time to consider because of how obvious it is is to use them as Mages. Would you make them the latest iteration of a group trying to remake the Nameless city? Or would they be true Pre Atlantis? Or Hell what is wrong with making Irem Atlantis? The default Shan'iatu seem to be remanents of a more Ancient Secret so they may even be from a prehuman civilization? Would you have them contain Archmages? Would they be Exarch Related? They could even be the Exarchs themselves, I wouldn't mind a story exploring that idea. </div> </div> </div>In the case of mages, I could posit Irem as part of the Ladder - not the Silver Ladder, the Atlantean one. In their bid to ascend to the Supernal, the Exarchs had to make ascension a powerful symbol with many expressions on Earth. So they founded civilisations in other regions (perhaps one for each path, Irem being the Moros one), each devoted to the metaphysical ascendancy of its leaders - in this case, the Shan'iatu wouldn't be Exarchs so much as proximi or sleepwalkers run by them - except that the Shan'iatu pulled off more than just the Exarch's purpose, and really achieved their own form of ascension. (In this case, Duat might be a realm on the far side of the Abyss, but not quite Stygia).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the Shan'iatu are the Maggot Host, Shartha that Father Wolf Chased into the Underworld. Perhaps they chose not become one and chose other goals for themselves, or perhaps they could not even become One, and thus had to decide another goal to fill their final drive. </div> </div> </div>I'd be inclined to go with a scorpion host rather than a maggot one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the Shan'iatu were simply Mortals with Supernatural Merits? Mortals can make Relics, and various supernatural merits can do a wide range of supernatural effects, particularly if they are long lived and have grown a vast amount of secrets. </div> </div> </div>The process that empowers relics from Reliquary have so many similarities to what Sekhem represents that it makes sense to consider them the same thing (just a bit more natural than the systematised artificial process the Shan'iatu developed). Thaumaturges are capable of most of what the Shan'iatu were capable of, at least before they embarked on making mummies and gods. Eternals from Immortals have the same connections to life, death, longevity, and crafted items. Freed from that rule about mixing templates, the Shan'iatu would make sense as Eternals capable of thaumaturgy and relic-making.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They could even have been a Hunter Conspiracy, After all we already have Relics as an Endowment, as well as Alchemy. Maybe they were something like a Conspiracy with 7 Conspiracies/Endowments working together. Hell I could see them having connections to the Aegis Kai, The Cheiron Group, and the Ascending Ones! Uter and Alchemy. </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine the write-ups for Aegis kai Doru and perhaps the Ascending Ones would have mentioned mummies had the game existed when Hunter was written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if they are Ghosts/Revanents from a fallen civilization? Using various Ghostly Numina and Influence, and cultivating Relics. Much like the Mortal option much can be explained with Relics, human nations turned to arcane ends, and the little cheat of Numina and Influence. </div> </div> </div>Ghosts and revenants who have found a way to function outside the Underworld, even without anchors - perhaps temporarily, and founded Irem the way it was in order to <i>make</i> it an anchor?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:31:03-07:00","id":112749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=112598#post112598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my own canon, they're aliens. Straight up. I don't know what the ramifications are of that and I'm not too worried about it. My planned long-term campaign even has a crystal skull of a Shan'iatu as being the crucial game-changing relic the <i>Mummy</i> world is going crazy for</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny when I next run Mummy I was planning on having the Shan'Iatu being aliens basically. I was going to fluff them as being from a &quot;higher dimension&quot; but getting invested in our own for reasons all their own. The Judges in this case are kinda gestalt Imago of the populace of Irem that are maintained by the Sekhem the Arisen find in our world. The Shan'Iatu created them to keep Ammut locked up. <br /> <br /> Weirdly similar at least with the whole &quot;alien&quot; thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=112598#post112598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably my favourite among the candidates from other game lines. Sineaters are more mystically powerful than the Shan'iatu appeared to be, but that could be refined to more mystically powerful <i>now</i>. Just as Irem was the first civilisation, perhaps the Shan'iatu were the first major krewe, and marked the beginning of the development of many of the Sineater powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, hold up. I don't think we can really make a judgement call on if any of the existing PC splats in the modern World of Darkness are more powerful then the Shan'Iatu. Seen as how everything we know about them is anecdotal and basically framed as a sorta vague creation legend. One that has undoubtedly been polluted by later cultures adding to the story and the general warped nature of the Arisen's memory's.<br /> <br /> We know that the Shan'Iatu were powerful magic users (we don't really even know what kind of magic they used, it likely involved Sekhem, a mystical resource that no modern day magic system seems to be aware of or able to manipulate) and that they got even more powerful after they went and made certain deals and did certain things in the great desert. That's it. Considering the Utterances the Arisen through around are hinted at being the baseline powers the Shan'Iatu had available to them, I' wiling to bet they were a lot more powerful then any PC splat save Mages who've hit Archmastery. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:12:09-07:00","id":113026,"title":"","content":"Aye, I'm pretty sure it's mentioned once or twice that Utterances are just rote-learned magic the Shan'iatu deigned to teach their servants. They refused to teach the basic principles of magic which would have allowed their followers to create their own spells (and/or discover the secret price of such magic), so it's more or less implied therefore that the Shan'iatu could wield free-form spells at least on the level of Utterances.<br /> <br /> That said, I do kind of like the idea of them as Sin Eaters (although I don't know too much about the game-line), with the Rite of Return being a really powerful Ceremony.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, the Book of Deceived will have rules for Mortal Sorcerers/Will Working and give us a better idea of what the Shan'iatu might have actually been like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T19:34:13-07:00","id":113070,"title":"","content":"Utterances are actually quite a strange thing. The one that summons a meteor, for example, is described like the Mummy is actually rewriting cosmic history billions of years ago in order to set up the situation where a meteor falls in the present time he 'summoned' it. The Arisen were never meant to wield Utterances, just as they were never meant to raise Memory or (maybe) return during a Sothic turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy: the Curse, pg. 17</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">More complex or overt powers are the province of Utterances\u2014magic spells wrested from the age of Irem. These powers can bind ghosts and wither flesh, and <b>although they can approach the power of the sorcerer-priests\u2019 own magic, their masters doubtless kept certain secrets for themselves</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. This implies that not only did the Shan'iatu have stronger spells, they also may have had different, unique magic of an entirely different nature. Remember, the Shan'iatu were the ones who performed the Rite of Return - the single strongest spell ever cast, able to eternally return the dead to life and render their gods and empire Nameless. Their Mummy servants are greater than they ever anticipated; so not only was it the greatest ritual ever cast, it was even greater than they imagined or intended","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T23:04:21-07:00","id":113149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=113070#post113070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This implies that not only did the Shan'iatu have stronger spells, they also may have had different, unique magic of an entirely different nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sesha-Hebsu entries in the Core book and in Guildhalls of the Deathless state much the same. The Sesha-Hebsu believe that magic is divided into two parts, the &quot;Will&quot; and the &quot;Word&quot;. The Sesha-Hebsu were created to be keepers of the &quot;Word&quot;, the formulaic aspect of magic, and some among them have memories that indicate the Lost Guild were keepers of the &quot;Will&quot;. Their theory is that this gave the Lost Guild too much knowledge about the nature of magic, which was why they had to be purged. Used in concert, the Word and the Will allowed the Shan'iatu to create spells from whole cloth, or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> Given the fact that the Lost Guild are Deathless creatures that somehow survived being purged before undergoing the Rite of Return, it would seem that the Sesha-Hebsu are at least partly on the right track there. The Deceived certainly learnt something that allowed them to endure an assault by the Shan'iatu, not to mention the 6,000 years since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T01:05:27-07:00","id":113188,"title":"","content":"Didn't you missed a few gamelines? Let me feel the blanks :P<br /> <br /> They were vampires. Through a special kind of Blood Sorcery, they learned how to feed upon life itself. Amut is their collective Beast, while the Judges are the manifestation of each of their inner Man in the vampiric underworld. They sacrificed many life to their Beast so they could make the human part of their soul to live forever. The Arisen were created through that complex &quot;Blood Sorcery&quot; which manipulate the energy of life itself in order to feed them forever and forever, until their hunger finally devoured Irem itself. And from those ruins, the vampires which survived swore to never let this act of blasphemy happen again, turning into the Akhud, all bound around a single rouge &quot;Judge&quot;- Shadad<br /> <br /> Only that its wrong. They were prometheans, driven by the messeges, visions and prophesies of powerful qashmalim. The Qashmliam were their Nameless Gods, and according to their will they built the whole empire- all in order to fulfill a single mission. Under their command, the Shan'iatu created a complex alchemic ritual which manipulate something more refined than even Azoth- Sekhem, the energy of life. Those rituals were used in order to give life to the Arisen, until the time has came and the prometheans has experienced a different form of &quot;New Dawn&quot;- Eternal Dusk. They became a new being, one which is made of eternal darkness and needs life energy in order to survive. That last transformation was powered by the complex geometry of Irem, and made it collapse all at once, as it was brought down with (heavenly) flames to turn the prometheans to something new, something more, something less- the Judges.<br /> <br /> No, no, you got it all wrong. They were stigmatics, which were pact bound to a great number of demons. The demons tried create Hell, free of the God Machine, and so they made an whole empire which was used as a &quot;free Infrastructure&quot;. In a way, it was an attempt of the demons to rebel against the God Machine by creating something only it should be able to do, and as such destroying its &quot;monopoly over reality&quot;. Yet, in order to do something so great, the demons needed a constant human sacrifice, and than they bound their souls to their service for all eternity. Surprisingly, their plan worked- and when the energies of the Infrastructure came to a peak, they took the souls and Covers of their human worshipers and terminated the project by binding the divine power to themselves, and thus becoming the Judges. Amut is their name to the God Machine, which keeps trying to absorb the rouge Infrastructure before it would take over its plannings and to return and become the only great power of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> That was almost right- the Shan'iatu were driven by demons, but not THOSE demons. Irem was an infernal empire, based around vice and hate. The Judges were demons from hell, which bound their Essence to the empire in order to not fall to Inferno because of their great power, while the Shan'iatu were possessed by them. The Arisen were the product of an attempt to make a world driven by vice forever and ever, and in that way to allow them to influence the world even after their empire would fall, Each mummy is the product of their infernal magics, and when Irem fell, the shards of their darkness are still found in the heart of each and every mummy. Through the complex scared geometry and cults, they are able to spread their infernal agenda, in hoping that one day they would turn the whole world into a true hell.<br /> <br /> But it is wring again. They were purified, which used their techniques to live forever and make this world into a better place. They spent decades at thinking what they should do in order to improve the world and refining their immortality techniques, until they managed to create an empire to bring order to the world and give immortality to their servants so they'll keep improving the world. In order to maintain their humanity, they consumed thousands of ghosts, until they finally became the Judges. Even today, they still try to improve the world though the Arisen- it is simply that their view about how a perfect world should be is radically different than the way most people now days see it.<br /> <br /> Actually, it's non of the above. The Shan'iatu were heroes- yes, heroes. People driven by such a passion that they turned into something more than human. Through that passion, they broke the laws of nature and gave life to the dead. Through that passion, they created a vast empire to glorify their name. Through that passion, they lived longer than any man should live. People has worshiped them, but they lived so long that the rhings people worshiped and what that they originally worshiped became different things- the Shan'iatu and the Judges. Finally, the Judges found the origin of their legends to be fallen, and the destroyed them and their whole empire- only to discover that without them, they have started to lose stability. In order to stop it, they used the Arisen to keep sustaining them, and by doing so to carry their own legend.<br /> <br /> Lies. All Lies. The empire of Irem was a lie. There are no Judges, no gods, nothing. They were just a group of tricky mortals, who managed to trick and whole nation. Eventually, like all empires, Irem fell- only to discover that by accident, they did something right- they actually did gave life to the dead. It was a flux, but the mummies don't know it. They only know the lies, which their own fervent minds keep following, believing them to be true. That means that every regular person upon the face of earth has a chance to create an Irem, and that even mortals can become gods- if they fuck it hard enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:42:37-07:00","id":113455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=112749#post112749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah, hold up. I don't think we can really make a judgement call on if any of the existing PC splats in the modern World of Darkness are more powerful then the Shan'Iatu. Seen as how everything we know about them is anecdotal and basically framed as a sorta vague creation legend. One that has undoubtedly been polluted by later cultures adding to the story and the general warped nature of the Arisen's memory's.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the likely tendency of such later rumour would be to inflate their power, not reduce it. So I'm ok with thinking they probably weren't inherently powerhouses - they <i>did</i> something very powerhouse-like (or two or three things), but the sense I get from the book is that this was a feat of planning and &quot;engineering&quot; way ahead of what they were &quot;ought&quot; to have been capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T12:16:05-07:00","id":113474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=112598#post112598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my own canon, they're aliens. Straight up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was implied pretty heavily in the Su Menent section of Guildhalls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T12:36:09-07:00","id":113485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=113455#post113455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the likely tendency of such later rumour would be to inflate their power, not reduce it. So I'm ok with thinking they probably weren't inherently powerhouses - they <i>did</i> something very powerhouse-like (or two or three things), but the sense I get from the book is that this was a feat of planning and &quot;engineering&quot; way ahead of what they were &quot;ought&quot; to have been capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your talking about the Rite of Return, the possible trans-location of Irem to Duat and the creation of 42 God-like beings I agree with you that these where not everyday feats the Shan'Iatu would be capable of pulling off. Those acts of magic are obviously the result of decades or centuries of planning and &quot;engineering&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still, to suggest that the Shan'Iatu were on the same level as the Second Sight version of Thaumaturges (not even a full &quot;racial&quot; template) is kinda silly. Considering the in-game and out of game sources of info we have on them (see Reseru and Azahul posts), they were throwing around Utterence level powers at minimum on a regular basis. With the implication being these were their most &quot;base&quot; magics and they have even greater magical might to call on if they wanted. <br /> <br /> I a believer in &quot;each to their own&quot; but in this case it takes some serious denial of the source material to come to the conclusion that the Shan'Iatu were basically &quot;nothing special&quot; when it comes to magic users in the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:52:15-07:00","id":114023,"title":"","content":"The Sorcerer-Kings (pre-evolution) had enough talent to have their <i>servants </i>learn all the currently known powers in the Mummy books. Mummies, pre-rite of return, were the equivalent to a ghoul or proximi to the 42 sorcerer-kings. If the servants had that much power, then the actual masters must have had more.<br /> <br /> Even more still, the source of their power is a powerful being (Apep) that is arguably at least on par with Luna, the Oracles, or a Deathlord.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, saying that one thing is more powerful than another is very misleading in this context. I tend to assume that all high-level beings are roughly equal in power. So tier 4 Archmasters are equal in power to Gentry, which are equal to Methuselah. <br /> <br /> <br /> I also tend to blend all the games into a few categories:<br /> <br /> Infernal - vampires and the inferno demons all come from the same region. Anything that survives via life draining some how.<br /> Shadow based - Anything from the Hisil, such as Purified, werewolves, and the ilk<br /> Underworld - pretty much anything ghostly, of which Geist is pretty much alone<br /> Astral/abyss/supernal - anything related to name magic tends to get an association here, <br /> Material world / God-Machine - Magic science and creationism. Genius, demon, prometheans.<br /> Faerie - so far, only changelings and other fae.<br /> <br /> Everything flows from one of these six realms/themes. Even hunter endowments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-16-2014, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:32:42-07:00","id":114051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=113485#post113485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I a believer in &quot;each to their own&quot; but in this case it takes some serious denial of the source material to come to the conclusion that the Shan'Iatu were basically &quot;nothing special&quot; when it comes to magic users in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not as much denial as it takes to read my original post and come to conclusion I was saying the Shan'iatu were nothing special.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:26:30-07:00","id":114087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114023#post114023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sorcerer-Kings (pre-evolution) had enough talent to have their <i>servants </i>learn all the currently known powers in the Mummy books. Mummies, pre-rite of return, were the equivalent to a ghoul or proximi to the 42 sorcerer-kings. If the servants had that much power, then the actual masters must have had more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, as mortal servants, I don't think the Arisen did have the books' powers. As I even stated in an above post, Utterances weren't even meant to be used by the Arisen; Affinities are powers endowed by the Rite of Return specifically so that the Arisen could carry out their purposes. I'm not saying that, as mortals in the Nameless Empire, the Arisen didn't use magic - indeed they did, but I think it was mostly alchemical in nature, which is exactly the kind of thing they can no longer do as Mummies!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114023#post114023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also tend to blend all the games into a few categories:<br /> <br /> Infernal - vampires and the inferno demons all come from the same region. Anything that survives via life draining some how.<br /> Shadow based - Anything from the Hisil, such as Purified, werewolves, and the ilk<br /> Underworld - pretty much anything ghostly, of which Geist is pretty much alone<br /> Astral/abyss/supernal - anything related to name magic tends to get an association here,<br /> Material world / God-Machine - Magic science and creationism. Genius, demon, prometheans.<br /> Faerie - so far, only changelings and other fae.<br /> <br /> Everything flows from one of these six realms/themes. Even hunter endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you put <i>Mummy</i>'s stuff? I fancy Duat as part of the Lower Depths, which Inferno is located in. Relics drain life experiences and knowledge and such from the world, shuankhsen and amkhata devour things all day, so it seems very &quot;life draining&quot; to me. I'm much broader in my cosmology, though, and consider the Shadow, Underworld, and Fae Arcadia all part of a 'Spirit World' that exists laterally with the material world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:37:29-07:00","id":114093,"title":"","content":"Hang on let me re-check your original post SunlessNick...<br /> <br /> Lets see: <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i><i>Sineaters are more mystically powerful than the Shan'iatu appeared to be&quot;</i><br /> <br /> \u200bPretty sure that this statement is intended to say that Sin Easters are more magically powerful then the Shan'Iatu were. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;the Shan'iatu wouldn't be Exarchs so much as proximi or sleepwalkers run by them&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Yeah because the proximi and sleepwalker mini-templates are not considered the weakest sub-template out of the major game lines. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'd be inclined to go with a scorpion host rather than a maggot one.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> \u200bAh hosts! The cannon fodder antagonists of Werewolf! To be fair they can be physically powerful, but nothing to off the charts. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The process that empowers relics from Reliquary have so many similarities to what Sekhem represents that it makes sense to consider them the same thing (just a bit more natural than the systematised artificial process the Shan'iatu developed). Thaumaturges are capable of most of what the Shan'iatu were capable of, at least before they embarked on making mummies and gods. Eternals from Immortals have the same connections to life, death, longevity, and crafted items. Freed from that rule about mixing templates, the Shan'iatu would make sense as Eternals capable of thaumaturgy and relic-making.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So the Shan'Iatu are comparable to a normal mortal with a 4-dot merit? Or a minor-template that is highly restricted in the way it does magic and can only use ritual casting? Or a type of immortal that gets access to about 3 supernatural traits? <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'd imagine the write-ups for Aegis kai Doru and perhaps the Ascending Ones would have mentioned mummies had the game existed when Hunter was written.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> OK, so the Relic or Elixer endowments, actually some pretty interesting effects in there at the higher end. Once again though, pretty anemic on the whole compared with other magic system in the NWoD. After all at the end of the day Endowments are just merits. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Ghosts and revenants who have found a way to function outside the Underworld, even without anchors - perhaps temporarily, and founded Irem the way it was in order to <i>make</i></i><i> it an anchor?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> What rank of Ghost? In fairness without that information you could be talking about rank 6+ ghosts and hell who knows what Numina can do at that point. <br /> <br /> Basically, every single comparison you made was with a character type that is &quot;nothing special&quot; in the Supernatural community of the NWoD. These things are something special among the human populace sure, I agree with you if that's your point. I was talking about entities within the supernatural aspect of the NWoD though in my arguments. As far as I can tell you compared the Shan'Iatu to exactly 1 major template (Sin Eaters) and did so in a negative fashion. Everything else is either merit based or a minor template. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I'd say you were arguaing that they were &quot;nothing special&quot; magically under the terms I've outlined above in your original post. Obviously the lack of tone and intimation present in written communication means I may have missed to deeper ambiguities you may have tried to include. If so its a failure of the method forum communication relies on. Sorry I grabbed the wrong end of the stick, we missed each other on this one. <br /> <br /> I don't mean to be a jerk on this, but its pretty obvious you either ignored or forgot (no big deal on that by the way, its a couple of sentences in a 270+ page book) the stuff that Reseru and Azahul dug out of the Core and Guildhall's books to you know...prove that the Shan'Iatu are on the same level as the Deathlords, Archmages and Methuselahs of the other game lines. Things that don't really have stats beyond &quot;what the ST says they have&quot; and are pretty far above even the peak PC's can hit with high power stats. <br /> <br /> Also bullshit like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114051#post114051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But not as much denial as it takes to read my original post and come to conclusion I was saying the Shan'iatu were nothing special.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for that man. Absolutely no need. <br /> <br /> You made an supposition based off of Eldagusto's premise, no issue. Reseru, Azahul and I pointed out section of the core fluff that provide a strong objective counter augment to one aspect of your premise. Once again no biggie. You counter-argued with a point that could apply to the cultural depiction of the Shan'Iatu (later cultures bigged them up as the basis for their own myths) but would not really impact on the supernatural/mystical aspect (Utterances are a known type of magic and the Scribes, Su-Mentet and Maa-Keep all independently have records of the epic stuff that the Shan'Iatu could pull magically) they had. I countered that if you wanted to go with the idea that the Shan'Iatu were pretty weak magically and comparable to the lower-tear (nothing special) magic users of the modern NWoD that it was doable but it required ignoring/removing the fluff that was counter to that supposition. You then made this personal for no good reason.<br /> <br /> I admit that I could have been clearer and less confrontational in my tone. I should have emphasized that if you want that idea to be the truth in your own games for example there is nothing wrong with having it play out that way. You know &quot;each to their own&quot; and embracing the toolbox idea of the NWoD and all that. I marginalized that aspect, to the detriment of this thread. Hell maybe at the time I'd had a crappy day, maybe I just did not think about what I was typing, I can't remember. <br /> <br /> With all the above being said I'd still say your reply was out-and-out and overreaction though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:23:58-07:00","id":114214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114087#post114087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, as mortal servants, I don't think the Arisen did have the books' powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also suggest that the pattern of the Empire's spread goes against the idea that the Shan'iatu were wielding greater powers than the Utterances - its technological and social innovations were just as critical to its ascendancy, which implies that the power of its magic didn't vastly surpass those things as game-changers. If the Shan'iatu were unique in their magic, I'm more inclined to suspect it was in their capacity to quasi-industrialise it, rather than it having sheer raw power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fancy Duat as part of the Lower Depths, which Inferno is located in. Relics drain life experiences and knowledge and such from the world, shuankhsen and amkhata devour things all day, so it seems very &quot;life draining&quot; to me. </div> </div> </div>It makes sense. Though I don't think relics take what they take out of the world in the sense of sending them into another world - what they take stays in the relic, to be used as its effect. But that's still <i>draining</i> of course, and mummies are tasked with sending the relics to Duat, which still makes them <i>tools</i> for removing experience and life from the world.<br /> <br /> It's also in keeping with Menat's characterisation of the whatever-the-hell-they found-in-the-desert as a mouth - though she seemed to think Sekhem was coming out of it, IIRC, rather than going in.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> One of the developers suggested a comparison between Sybaris and Disquiet, and we haven't looked at Promethean yet. A not dissimilar comparison could be made with relic curses and the Wasteland. In both cases, the causes and purposes seem to be different, but neither creature entirely understands their condition.<br /> <br /> Could the Divine Fire be used to materialise a different kind of vision than the one of creating life? Rather than Prometheans, something like demiurges.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114023#post114023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sorcerer-Kings (pre-evolution) had enough talent to have their <i>servants </i>learn all the currently known powers in the Mummy books. Mummies, pre-rite of return, were the equivalent to a ghoul or proximi to the 42 sorcerer-kings. If the servants had that much power, then the actual masters must have had more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't follow. As <b>reseru</b> said, mummies' current powers are a result of the Rite, and bringing up Promethean again, the Created are capable of much that demiurges are not.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114093#post114093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also bullshit like this: ... No need for that man. Absolutely no need.</div> </div> </div> </div>You opened that door.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, every single comparison you made was with a character type that is &quot;nothing special&quot; in the Supernatural community of the NWoD </div> </div> </div>Actually, no. If you look back at where I mentioned thaumaturges, I suggested they could have been thaumaturges <i>and</i> relic-makers <i>and</i> eternals. Ie, something which is according to the standard rules a mix of templates and impossible. That's pretty special.<br /> <br /> I would also note that special can cover a lot more than just being vastly powerful. Look back at my paragraph in response to reseru. The Shan'iatu industrialised their magic, and seemed to be able to use it as reliably and repeatably as technology. Frankly, I find that <i>more</i> special than just another mystic giant. Also, the parts of the books that imply they were mystic giants are those written firmly from the point of view of the Arisen whose minds and memories were scrambled (and who have a built-in veneration to contend with). I put more stock in Menat's account, which has the greater part of their <i>power</i> coming from an external source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T16:22:52-07:00","id":114397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114214#post114214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense. Though I don't think relics take what they take out of the world in the sense of sending them into another world - what they take stays in the relic, to be used as its effect. But that's still <i>draining</i> of course, and mummies are tasked with sending the relics to Duat, which still makes them <i>tools</i> for removing experience and life from the world.<br /> <br /> It's also in keeping with Menat's characterisation of the whatever-the-hell-they found-in-the-desert as a mouth - though she seemed to think Sekhem was coming out of it, IIRC, rather than going in.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> One of the developers suggested a comparison between Sybaris and Disquiet, and we haven't looked at Promethean yet. A not dissimilar comparison could be made with relic curses and the Wasteland. In both cases, the causes and purposes seem to be different, but neither creature entirely understands their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that bit about relics is what I understood and hoped to convey. They drain from this world and then Mummies bring the relics back to Duat. And uh...I fancy as Prometheans originating from the Lower Depths as well, so funny you should bring that bit back up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, they're Lower Depth entities who, like Mages, have a special affinity with the dimension 'above' them. Demiurges 'summon' the Lower Depth entity into this world, and the vague powers of the Divine Fire grant them life. Pandorans, like most creatures from that emptier plane, seek only to devour and destroy. Disquiet happens because people are naturally freaked by something so alien, and Wasteland happens because the very world is freaked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:22:19-07:00","id":114723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114087#post114087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, as mortal servants, I don't think the Arisen did have the books' powers. As I even stated in an above post, Utterances weren't even meant to be used by the Arisen; Affinities are powers endowed by the Rite of Return specifically so that the Arisen could carry out their purposes. I'm not saying that, as mortals in the Nameless Empire, the Arisen didn't use magic - indeed they did, but I think it was mostly alchemical in nature, which is exactly the kind of thing they can no longer do as Mummies!</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, they might not have used Utterances, as that required a steady supply of magic power, which the Sorcerer-Kings didn't reveal the secret of. That said, if they were given a battery of such magic, I think they could have been taught Utterances to use. Naturally, Mummies come with a large store of magic power inside them, so the batteries are no longer necessary. <br /> <br /> As well, the servants did, and still do, use alchemy - the problem is that such alchemy has a strong necromatic vibe. All of Irem's magic came from twisted, dark powers in some way. And many of its technological achievements were based on this profane magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where do you put <i>Mummy</i>'s stuff? I fancy Duat as part of the Lower Depths, which Inferno is located in. Relics drain life experiences and knowledge and such from the world, shuankhsen and amkhata devour things all day, so it seems very &quot;life draining&quot; to me. I'm much broader in my cosmology, though, and consider the Shadow, Underworld, and Fae Arcadia all part of a 'Spirit World' that exists laterally with the material world </div> </div> </div> First, let me say that DaveB, big time mage developer, has said that Duat is part of the Lower Depths, as is the Inferno, and whatever the shadowy place the Strix come from is. So, that's official. I just like a more united cosmology, so I change and combine some things - everything below is my alterations to the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> I put Mummy under Name magic, as that's actually a theme through the game, I notice. The NAMEless empire, anyone? Utterances (speaking words?) The lost guild's specialty? Inscription amulets? As well, Duat has a ton in common with the Abyss, I feel - it resonates strongly with how the Sorcerer-King magic works. Especially given that, to become a Mummy, you undergo a process similar to an astral journey, but far more torturous.<br /> <br /> As well, if you read my post in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/105380-filing-off-the-serial-numbers\">Filing off the Serial Numbers</a> thread, you'll see how I talk about how I see the fundamental story of Mummy is one of &quot;servant to a dread necromancer building an empire with their magic.&quot; Its a lot like the high fantasy plot of the evil necromancer raising armies of undead to take over the world. Said necromancers are almost invariably a kind of mage instead of a glorified ghost or vampire.<br /> <br /> I just feel that Mummy magic, stories, and themes just have too much in common with Mage magic, stories, and themes for me to not group them together in my personal cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-17-2014, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:35:19-07:00","id":114729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114397#post114397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And uh...I fancy as Prometheans originating from the Lower Depths as well, so funny you should bring that bit back up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My 2 cents - I read a thing in the God Machine Chronicle book, an off hand possibility that the Principle is a rogue element of the God Machine that went its own way long ago. So, in my personal cosmology, the Principle is Lucifer himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:55:12-07:00","id":114734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114723#post114723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, let me say that DaveB, big time mage developer, has said that Duat is part of the Lower Depths, as is the Inferno, and whatever the shadowy place the Strix come from is. So, that's official. I just like a more united cosmology, so I change and combine some things - everything below is my alterations to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that the Lower Depths are more of a classification than a collection of related realms; it's a term that means &quot;a realm that Mages basically have no clue about that seems to be further away from the Supernal than the Fallen World.&quot;<br /> <br /> Incidentally - and on topic - if you stuck a gun to my head and told me I had to write out an origin for the Shan'iatu for my home games, I'd say that they were originally mortal thaumaturgists/priests who stumbled into the right place and right time and in the pursuit of more power swung waaaaay above their paygrade and connected the human world to Duat*, providing a weird and unique source of power that eventually shaped them into the grand necromancers they were. The rest, as they say, is history.<br /> <br /> * which incidentally in my game is also where the Strix came from - the Shan'iatu unwittingly loosed them into the world, and even during it's height the Nameless Empire constantly pushed back against the blood-hungry demons in the nearby wastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 04-17-2014, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T09:27:43-07:00","id":114746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114397#post114397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fancy as Prometheans originating from the Lower Depths as well, so funny you should bring that bit back up ... Disquiet happens because people are naturally freaked by something so alien, and Wasteland happens because the very world is freaked</div> </div> </div> </div>I also see Disquiet as the psyche being &quot;burned&quot; not dissimilarly to how the Wasteland &quot;burns&quot; the land - hence why it can affect the victim's relationships with other people besides the Promethean. Which means it ties in even better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114723#post114723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, the servants did, and still do, use alchemy - the problem is that such alchemy has a strong necromatic vibe. All of Irem's magic came from twisted, dark powers in some way. And many of its technological achievements were based on this profane magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their sorcery, spirituality, alchemy, and technology weren't terribly distinct in any case. (Incidentally this is one reason why I'd count mages well down the list of likely candidates for the Shan'iatu; mages' magic is about transcending this world, which Sekhem-based magic is very much <i>of</i> this world).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, let me say that DaveB, big time mage developer, has said that Duat is part of the Lower Depths, as is the Inferno, and whatever the shadowy place the Strix come from is. So, that's official. </div> </div> </div>Huh, I didn't know he'd said that about Duat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just like a more united cosmology, so I change and combine some things - everything below is my alterations to the game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, me too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just feel that Mummy magic, stories, and themes just have too much in common with Mage magic, stories, and themes for me to not group them together in my personal cosmology. </div> </div> </div>And the Abyss gets round the dichotomy I mentioned in my previous paragraph. While it corrupts, bends, and warps what it touches, that applies to itself too - to maintain the coherence of a realm like Duat and entities like the Judges, power from this world would be to its benefit.<br /> <br /> So far, we've been talking about who and to a lesser extent how. But why is a question, too. We know the Shan'iatu wanted an empire, and going by Menat they wanted to become gods, and sacrificed the empire to that end. (Her account is slightly ambiguous, though, on whether they founded their empire <i>for the purpose</i> of sacrificing it, or decided it was expendable later on). So how would these motives line up with different games?<br /> <br /> Sineaters: Several of the archetypes are associated with judgment (especially reapers), preparing people for death (especially pilgrims), and maintaining order between life and death (especially gatekeepers). If a krewe's philosophy were formed around a fusion of these three, then could Irem have been an especially grandiose exercise in carrying them out? Put the people into rigid niches that lead to predictable (and thus usable) ghostly echoes? What would they sacrifice it for? Unless they felt their ends coming, and weren't confident about any possible successors - sineaters are durable, but not infinitely so - and wanted their creation to outlast them. So they made it a death realm, and created mummies to carry on their work in the living world. That would suggest that it's the exercise of judgement on behalf of the judges and glorifying Irem that's the more important purpose than sending relics to Duat.<br /> <br /> With the idea of ghosts and revenants from a former civilisation, their motive would presumably be about recreating as much of what they'd lost as possible - creating Irem and the empire as a giant, mutual anchor for themselves, maybe. Until they conceived of becoming deathlords and/or kerberoi and turned it into a dead dominion instead - perhaps creating the mummies as replacement anchors. Also, either sineaters or geists could be from the aforementioned civilisation, combining this with the previous paragraph.<br /> <br /> Mages: I can't think of a reason beyond what I've already suggested.<br /> <br /> Changelings: If the Fae were behind the fall of the empire, it would imply a massive kidnapping - perhaps by a Keeper who wanted to play at being a god-king. But nothing like that's happened before or since that we know of, implying that it would normally be beyond the Fae to accomplish it. So either the empire was owed to them in some way - did they provide power to the Shan'iatu, or did that thing the Shan'iatu found belong to the Fae in some way? Or the Fae provided something to pay for it - and the mummies might be that. Given that time goes weirdly in Arcadia, it opens up the possibility of an Iremite changeling.<br /> <br /> Mortals: Lines up by itself. Long, grand projects are frequently the province of mortals in the WoD after all, and they're the ones with the most motive to elevate themselves. I don't really see what would motivate hunters as Hunter depicts them, though.<br /> <br /> LostLight came up with a good motives for vampires for the gamelines he covered.<br /> <br /> Though regarding Prometheans, the empire could have been a vast Pilgrimmage: despairing of achieving humanity through &quot;normal&quot; routes, they tried to remake humanity in a mould they could then fill.<br /> <br /> Finally, what about Claimed? Perhaps there had been thousands of people who'd had small dreams of the things Irem came to embody - giving rise to small, weak spirits of those things. Who then banded together to create a concrete example of their concepts to increase their own power and meaning. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T14:57:09-07:00","id":114954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=114723#post114723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, they might not have used Utterances, as that required a steady supply of magic power, which the Sorcerer-Kings didn't reveal the secret of. That said, if they were given a battery of such magic, I think they could have been taught Utterances to use. Naturally, Mummies come with a large store of magic power inside them, so the batteries are no longer necessary.<br /> <br /> As well, the servants did, and still do, use alchemy - the problem is that such alchemy has a strong necromatic vibe. All of Irem's magic came from twisted, dark powers in some way. And many of its technological achievements were based on this profane magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> First, let me say that DaveB, big time mage developer, has said that Duat is part of the Lower Depths, as is the Inferno, and whatever the shadowy place the Strix come from is. So, that's official. I just like a more united cosmology, so I change and combine some things - everything below is my alterations to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies don't really do a whole lot of alchemy, though. Kepher is the closest thing they have that remains of their possible older talents. The bit in the core describing Apotheosis lays out pretty clearly that one of its benefits is that you can put Sekhem into an object - effectively creating a relic, which is what they did as mortals. Otherwise the only thing they can do now is find vessels. In the old forums there were several people that complained it was dumb that the Arisen were once these grand alchemists but now they could do, basically, nothing with it.<br /> <br /> I save anything about the Lower Depths that a developer says. Here's a shortened DaveB quote, just the paragraph about Duat:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Awakened terms, The Inferno of WoD: Inferno is one of the Depths - the beings in it feed on sin, and it's reached through Irises punctured into Shadow-world Wounds. Mages who studied the Arisen and interviewed mummies who were capable of and inclined to give descriptions of what happened to them, would probably conclude that Duat is one of the Depths, too. And that goes double for wherever the Strix are from.</div> </div> </div> </div>In no way would I say that's 'official' especially considering 1) it'll never be written into a <i>Mummy</i> book and 2) he's not the <i>Mummy</i> developer. Now, I respect and obsess over the man's head-canon and am fond of putting Duat as a Depth but...certainly not official. We'll go with &quot;fanon.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There was another post he made, though, that I don't have saved where he said Duat might not be part of the Depths, and rather that's just where Mages would conclude it is because Mages have a tendency to put dangerous, out-of-context-magic things that they don't like into the Depths as a sort of &quot;bin of unorganized stuff.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's another DaveB quote, that consequentially might be seen as 'official':<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy doesn't mention Awakened Mages at all - its &quot;sorcerers&quot; are not Mages, the Shan'iatu were not Mages, and Alantis was not one of the rival empires Irem fought.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T18:16:30-07:00","id":115055,"title":"","content":"Reserve, Lower Depths is a Mage term for distant, dark realms to begin with. Saying that something is Lower Depths means nothing outside of Mage, and very little in. It's not anything specific the rest of the WoD cares about, certainly not vamps, hunters, or mummies. So, the mage writer is the only one who COULD have said it. Not like it matters to me in the long run, since I combined strix and inferno together in my mind, along with shoving duat into the astral/abyss for my stuff. And &quot;lower depth&quot; is now an alternative name for the inferno to whitewash it for dabblers. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T18:21:39-07:00","id":115056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=115055#post115055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reserve, Lower Depths is a Mage term for distant, dark realms to begin with. Saying that something is Lower Depths means nothing outside of Mage, and very little in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember being excited for about five minutes when I noticed how much of the cosmology the Lower Depths seemed to explain.<br /> <br /> It was a more innocent time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T18:54:01-07:00","id":115063,"title":"","content":"First thing I noticed when I saw the mage cosmology was &quot;Its nearly an exact copy/paste from the oWoD cosmology.&quot; I kinda figured that the Lower Depths would have been a demon-home, like it was in oWoD with the area below the Lower Umbra. <br /> <br /> Now that nWoD is all grown up and its own thing, I wouldn't be surprised if the entire idea behind Lower Depths just kinda... goes away, honestly. We have rules for strix, infernal things, and kinda-duat stuff in the respective game lines, and mages trying to summon random crazy shit from Out There don't need such a vague umbrella term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T19:09:07-07:00","id":115068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=115063#post115063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that nWoD is all grown up and its own thing, I wouldn't be surprised if the entire idea behind Lower Depths just kinda... goes away, honestly. We have rules for strix, infernal things, and kinda-duat stuff in the respective game lines, and mages trying to summon random crazy shit from Out There don't need such a vague umbrella term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly hope it <i>does</i><i>n't</i> go away, what with the ten thousand hells floating around just past the shadow of the world being an evocative bit of mental shorthand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T19:20:19-07:00","id":115072,"title":"","content":"Well, we'll see eventually. I'm not expecting too much, however, going forwards. I feel like we've reached a saturation point in the World of Darkness, and much of what we get from here on out is going to be covering a lot of material other games do. Like I said, Mummy shares a lot in common with Mage. Promethean with Demon. The Inferno and Vampire. More and more, I feel like there's so much overlap between games, and less and less new space being explored; just new twists on the old stuff. Sure, you can create a new realm of animistic spirits doing things, and it'll be different from the Hisil so as to have its own realm, but does it need to be?<br /> <br /> <br /> I look at it like this - changelings and mages both access the same dream world. However, they do it in such mind boggling, vastly different ways that they might as well be different. I think that all these realms could be interconnected rather than individual playgrounds; however, each supernatural gets a different view of the pie. Qashmallim and angels could be the same beings, just seen from different angles. An infernal whisper could be a variant strix (or the other way around) that infects spirits instead of physical bodies. And so on.<br /> <br /> That's why I like thinking of the Judges as uber-necromancers of fantasy with their undead armies. They see and access the astral / supernal / abyssal space differently than the Awakened, and learned to steal power from living beings from contact with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T00:57:19-07:00","id":115158,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is any problem with Duat being classified as a &quot;Lower Depth&quot; by mages. The &quot;Lower Depths&quot; is simply a term to define any realm which is &quot;metaphysically distant&quot; from the Supernal Realms, and as such it is harder for mages to effect it. Dave once said that the reason mages give such shiny and big names to things it is in order to claim that they understand them- even if they don't. In short, the Lower Depths is simply a term for realms that mages don't know much about them, and don't really have power upon them- and Duat seems to answer that definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T04:04:39-07:00","id":115201,"title":"","content":"You know, there is actually another game I would do the whole origins story thing with, again. The God-Machine / Demon /Promethean. Mummies are Created beings, just like Prometheans and Angels. All the games have a strong vibe that deals with godly beings, evolution of the self, and breaking free of the chains of slavery of your master.<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess, what it comes down to for me, is that there are three things going for mummy:<br /> 1) Name magic, magical empires, magic cults.<br /> 2) Created servants<br /> 3) Undead army and emphasis on the past<br /> <br /> The first lends itself to mage stuff, the second to promethean themes, the third to ghostly stuff. I could see tying it to any one of those, easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-18-2014, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T16:29:11-07:00","id":115585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=115158#post115158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there is any problem with Duat being classified as a &quot;Lower Depth&quot; by mages. The &quot;Lower Depths&quot; is simply a term to define any realm which is &quot;metaphysically distant&quot; from the Supernal Realms, and as such it is harder for mages to effect it. Dave once said that the reason mages give such shiny and big names to things it is in order to claim that they understand them- even if they don't. In short, the Lower Depths is simply a term for realms that mages don't know much about them, and don't really have power upon them- and Duat seems to answer that definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy put what I was trying to say a little better. In-universe, at the very least, Mages aren't even sure there is a lower, emptier, more distant, hungrier realm. They just see malicious, hungry creatures and say, &quot;Wow, I wonder where all these hungry things come from. Maybe there's a Hungry Realm? Maybe we'll be pretentious and call it, 'Lower Depths!'&quot; When they see Mummies they aren't saying, &quot;Ah, yes. We know they're from the Lower Depths because we're Mages and know everything.&quot; They're saying, &quot;What the hell is this thing talking about?! It's giving me the heeby jeebies, just like things from the Hungry Realm do.&quot;<br /> <br /> But correlation-oriented conclusions are shaky at best <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T10:20:00-07:00","id":115937,"title":"","content":"Has anyone officially said Duat is <i>not</i> part of the nWoD Underworld? I'm just curious whether there's any reason it can't be one of the old dominions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T12:19:46-07:00","id":116022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=115937#post115937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone officially said Duat is <i>not</i> part of the nWoD Underworld? I'm just curious whether there's any reason it can't be one of the old dominions.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRRC, no, there is no such statement that Duat is not a Dead Dominion. Actually, there was even a theory that the Judges are simply 42 Kereboi working together in the same dominion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T11:08:24-07:00","id":116590,"title":"","content":"Storyteller spoilers<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The fact that the small mockup &quot;Pillars&quot; from irem basically function as ghost repelling forcefields says to me that they were planning on dropping Irem into a place with lots of ghosts and generally hostile deathly environments, and needed a shield. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T17:43:37-07:00","id":116760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=116590#post116590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyteller spoilers<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The fact that the small mockup &quot;Pillars&quot; from irem basically function as ghost repelling forcefields says to me that they were planning on dropping Irem into a place with lots of ghosts and generally hostile deathly environments, and needed a shield. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I like that one.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Isn't the Curse for those same relics that the ghosts in contact with them for long periods grow deformed and powerful? A Dominion filled with mutant ghosts wielding Utterance-like Numen could be fun...</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:52:54-07:00","id":116889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=116022#post116022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IRRC, no, there is no such statement that Duat is not a Dead Dominion. Actually, there was even a theory that the Judges are simply 42 Kereboi working together in the same dominion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That raises the terrifying question of -<br /> <br /> &quot;What the hell is Ammut?&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Judges are &quot;just&quot; Kereboi and their creation required a &quot;deal&quot; with Ammut that implies she's a damn sight more powerful then them. I guess the dull answer is a Death Lord. I kinda like the idea of &quot;The First Cthonian or The Mother o Cthonians&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T08:06:42-07:00","id":116948,"title":"","content":"That might make for a fun time, too! There is an Utterance which lets you summon a cthonian (which the <i>Summoners </i>supplement for <i>Mage</i> says some cthonians know how to reach the Lower Depths, whatever that implies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) so perhaps Ammut is related","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:17:42-07:00","id":147919,"title":"","content":"Actually, I know what the city of Duat is and who it was made by. IanW was on table top games talking about Duat....well hinting at it. Dave (mage developer) and IanW were discussing the [REDACTED] City, which is located in Egypt. It is replacing Atlantis as the starting origin for mage - the fallen world chronicle. Duat is the capital city of the [REDACTED] Empire, which created the mummies to return all Relics back to it. Essential, Atlantis is myth. Kinda..to quote Dave, atlantis is the city that was, but is not anymore! Mages edited reality to erase it and remove its existence. Now we have Duat (as the mummies know it), but the mages will call it [REDACTED].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3116-morkizga","user":"morkizga","date":". 05-24-2014, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3116-morkizga","name":"morkizga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:33:07-07:00","id":147940,"title":"","content":"So yeah, mages of great power (Gods) became our beloved Judges and we the faithful serve them for all time. What really scrambles my noodle....have we always served them....as we descend into the underworld....are we really ascending back to the beginning before the fallen world and becoming members of the Atlantis that was but isn't anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3116-morkizga","name":"morkizga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T11:08:18-07:00","id":147977,"title":"","content":"I...what?<br /> <br /> There's no 'official' crossover, whatever Dave or Ian's head-canon or inter-game napkin scrawls might imply, and all of your 'redacted' I think we all know. After all, <i>Mummy</i> has been out for a year. Not that I doubt the <i>Fallen World Chronicle</i> might present Atlantis differently, it's still 'Atlantis' in that it's a wonderful, ancient Mage-empire that's no more, but we all know it's not Atlantis as Plato envisioned and more the archetype of 'fallen Mage empire' anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T11:37:04-07:00","id":147987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=116889#post116889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That raises the terrifying question of -<br /> <br /> &quot;What the hell is Ammut?&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Judges are &quot;just&quot; Kereboi and their creation required a &quot;deal&quot; with Ammut that implies she's a damn sight more powerful then them. I guess the dull answer is a Death Lord. I kinda like the idea of &quot;The First Cthonian or The Mother o Cthonians&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal theory is that Ammut <i>is</i> Duat.<br /> <br /> The Judges aren't demanding Sekhem from the living world because they're greedy or (power-)hungry or have some kind of complicated scheme that needs lots of Sekhem to fuel it. They <i>n</i><i>eed</i> it to survive inside of the worldscape-innards of a cosmic personification of hunger.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I mean, look at what the core's Storyteller section has to say about what the Shan'iatu found in the desert. A mouth opened wide to the sky, and a Sekhem-filled gullet and stomach below...it sounds like they found Ammut right there, <i>in this world.</i> Not in Duat.<br /> <br /> Ammut is the sarlacc pit writ large, and Duat is her stomach.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 05-24-2014, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T17:11:38-07:00","id":148267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=147987#post147987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I mean, look at what the core's Storyteller section has to say about what the Shan'iatu found in the desert. A mouth opened wide to the sky, and a Sekhem-filled gullet and stomach below...it sounds like they found Ammut right there, <i>in this world.</i> Not in Duat.<br /> <br /> Ammut is the sarlacc pit writ large, and Duat is her stomach.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh, I like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T19:13:53-07:00","id":148329,"title":"","content":"In my world, the Shan'iatu and the God-Machine are inextricably linked. See, back in the mists of time the space faring ship of an ancient race brought SOMETHING here. It was the first Infrastructure on Earth. When their ship crashed, it turned into the first. The aliens made, or maybe worshiped, some kind of God of technology. This was the God-Machine. When the Aliens ventured out, they educated the primitive humans, turning them into a great Empire. The shan'iatu sold themselves to alien gods in a bid to escape their old Master, and become one among the gods.<br /> <br /> Or something like that. As disciples, or possibly creators, of the God-Machine, the aliens had knowledge of occult physics. They made pacts with the Nameless gods, and... well, the rest is history. At least in my world. I haven't worked on the misty past too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T19:50:57-07:00","id":148343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=147977#post147977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I...what?<br /> <br /> There's no 'official' crossover, whatever Dave or Ian's head-canon or inter-game napkin scrawls might imply, and all of your 'redacted' I think we all know. After all, <i>Mummy</i> has been out for a year. Not that I doubt the <i>Fallen World Chronicle</i> might present Atlantis differently, it's still 'Atlantis' in that it's a wonderful, ancient Mage empire that's no more, but we all know it's not Atlantis as Plato envisioned and more the archetype of 'fallen Mage empire' anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>Unnnn Huh...bet you are wrong.. Fallen world changes the Atlantis format....Dave strikes me as a serious history buff...based upon his few short remarks and IanW's....Atlantis is LITERALLY no more. It will not be default point of origin. IT will be the [REDACTED] city based in Egypt. The city will be based upon Persia, Egypt and one other culture. So, mages want talk about Atlantis this Atlantis that....they will speak of this city.<br /> <br /> By the way...what is the name of [REDACTED] city?<br /> *SNICKER*<br /> <br /> The cities name is not Duat by the way....it has another name the mages shall call it by!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3116-morkizga","name":"morkizga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T20:06:01-07:00","id":148351,"title":"","content":"Well, either you're givin' away information you shouldn't, or, you are lying. Either way, the future will hold the truth. It's not a bad idea, per se, to have a model of a city that modern Mages think when they think 'Atlantis', but even in that time they were still searching for the mythical FIRST CITY, but I'm not sure if I take your word on it being canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:02:35-07:00","id":148385,"title":"","content":"I just...the thing is that Mages don't necessarily believe mage!Atlantis is plato!Atlantis anyway. The Supernal is about archetypes and symbolism; mage!Atlantis just symbolizes the idea of a 'ancient, fallen empire where Mages practiced openly and powerfully.' It's about the time before the Seers did a cosmic retcon on the universe.<br /> <br /> While I can see <i>FWC</i> maybe changing up the mythos a bit, I wonder how necessary it is; this isn't a decade ago when everyone hated mage!Atlantis, there's no need to change it to something 'more appealing.'<br /> <br /> And half of your redacted stuff just sounds like you're giving away <i>Mummy</i> spoilers from two years ago. &quot;The [REDACTED] Empire&quot;? I'm willing to bet is &quot;The Nameless Empire&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:28:49-07:00","id":148393,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect this is more blather confusing FWC with To The Strongest again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T01:11:00-07:00","id":148519,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect you're right. Because there's still Irem in Mummy, and the Awakened City in the Time Before is still in Mage. Modern mages even mostly still call it Atlantis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T03:05:53-07:00","id":148557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/112142-crossover-brainstorm-various-shan-iatu-origins?p=148519#post148519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strongly suspect you're right. Because there's still Irem in Mummy, and the Awakened City in the Time Before is still in Mage. Modern mages even mostly still call it Atlantis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the manipulations of certain Archmagi, they could be correct.<br /> <br /> Damn Archmagi, everything made sense but no, they have to constantly remake the cosmology.<br /> <br /> This is my reasoning why there won't ever be a &quot;complete&quot; map of nWoD.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}